  "id": "social-memory",
  "term": "social memory",
  "definition": "Social memory is memory for prior social experience, commonly studied with social discrimination procedures in which an animal is familiarized and then tested after a delay. In this literature, it is discussed as short-term when examined over minutes and as long-term when assessed over longer intervals, with evidence that these forms rely on different mechanisms.",
